8f7d22dac11537294b71b50c9c2f"},{"path":"src/FS.GG.SDD.Commands/ProviderCapabilityAdmission.fs","repository":"FS-GG/FS.GG.SDD","revision":"c1fee66a34ec8d222586eb708ddff4973ad5594e","sha256":"e887b15222c87604332c6d73a759fbc7016fb9261ed1ce8965a9cc224a34747d"}],"conflictsWith":[],"id":"governance/provider-verify-sdd-codec-skew","kind":"decision","recordedAt":"2026-10-23T08:27:00Z","repository":"FS-GG/FS.GG.Governance","schema":"fsgg.atlas/1","status":"recorded","summary":"Governance's provider-mode Verify decodes schema-2 scaffold provenance and the independent policy with the bundled SDD Commands/Artifacts 2.3.0 packages. It admits provenance produced by SDD 2.4.0. Decision (GOV-423-C2, PR #472): keep the 2.3.0 pin. The wire contract is the closed schema-2 provenance codec, the CatalogScaffoldPolicy parser and ProviderCapabilityAdmission, not the producer package version. ScaffoldProvenanceDocument, CatalogScaffoldProvenance, CatalogScaffoldPolicy and ProviderCapabilityAdmission are byte-identical between SDD 2.3.0 (c8aea928) and 2.4.0 (c1fee66a). On that path the only 2.4.0 change is #1116, which changes the scaffold's template override argv encoding; that argv is recorded data. A future codec change is refused by the strict parsers rather than misread. Moving the bundled pair is a separate Governance release decision; re-check the codec modules whenever SDD publishes a new version.","supersedes":[],"tags":["governance","sdd","provenance","version","compatibility","verify"],"title":"Verify keeps the bundled SDD 2.3.0 provenance codec while admitting SDD 2.4.0 provenance"}
